      {
        "_uid": "e1b0461a-9559-0756-ccee-09bc025ca0fb",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Microforests",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "bold"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Fully in the theme of land restoration, AKU has initiated microforests on five of its campuses, in the cities of Nairobi, Dar-as-Salam, Arusha, Kampala, and Karachi. A microforest is a small, dense, biodiverse forest, in which at least 25 local species are planted very close together on a small piece of land; this is known as the Miyawaki method. The dense plantation has shown to support quick upwards growth of trees as they compete for sunlight.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Microforests offer a range of environmental, social, and economic benefits. Environmentally, they contribute to biodiversity by providing habitats for various plants, insects, birds, and other wildlife. They help sequester carbon, thus mitigating climate change, and improve air quality by filtering pollutants. Microforests also enhance soil health and water retention, reducing the risk of flooding and soil erosion. Not only do microforests rehabilitate land but they also inspire a deeper connection between people and nature. In the planting of these microforests at university campuses, AKU has engaged its own students, partner institutions, and local communities.",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
